-Owner skill: `skill://rust-conventions`. The AI's workspace for one range window started with `--ai` (plan §2 #108–#111, #115, #122): its temporary checkout of the right commit and the agent process running in it; Rust never reads the agent's messages (ACP is the window's). `lib.rs` (the IPC types `AgentRun`, `AgentCommand`, `AgentStartReply`, `CheckoutReply`, `CheckoutLook` — serde tag `kind`, variants as named; `Error`; `HostEvent` re-exported from `yamt-pipe`, so the shell takes the agent's events from this crate), `workspace.rs` (`Pair` from `yamt-range`'s pair lock; `Workspace`: `prepare` makes or reuses `<pair folder>/checkout`, `start` only after `prepare` with cwd = the checkout and a running agent stopped and reaped first — it blocks up to about 3 s for that —, `send`/`stop` for the current run only, `stop_agent`, `look_job`, `discard` and `end(self)` stop and reap the agent before any removal (only the agent's own process, never one it started), `sweep_leftovers(&mut self, range_dir)` the one writer of this pair's leftovers besides `prepare`), `checkout.rs` (`checkout_folder` the one checkout path; made as `checkout.partial` — `clone --shared --no-checkout`, `remote remove origin`, `checkout --detach` the right commit — then renamed to `checkout`, so a `checkout/` is always complete; removed through `checkout.removing` (`set_aside`, then `remove_set_aside`); `remove_when_clean`; a folder another remover deletes at the same time counts as removed), `look.rs` (`LookJob::look`: `Missing`, `Clean`, `Changed` = any `git status` entry, ignored files never, any branch or `refs/stash` (`refs`, #122: the clone starts with none), or `HEAD` ≠ the right commit; `Unreadable` when git fails or finds another repository than the checkout's own; git through `Repo::discover_from_folder`, never an inherited `GIT_DIR`), `process.rs` (the program through `yamt_pipe::find` without project entries — PATH, then the command's home folders; a relative path with a separator is refused as `NotFound { searched: [] }`, it would run a file of the reviewed commit — and `Running::start_without` with `Framing::Lines` and `yamt_gitio::Repo::REPOSITORY_VARIABLES` left out of the agent's environment), `sweep.rs` (every other pair folder holding a checkout or a leftover, skipped without its lock otherwise; under the lock `PairLock::try_hold` takes: the partial and removing folders deleted and a clean checkout renamed to `checkout.removing`, deleted after the lock is released; a changed or unreadable one kept; the right commit from `yamt_range::pair_right_commit`). `bin/agent-echo.rs`: the tests' line agent (echo, `pwd`, `edit <file>`, `exit <code>`, `hold <file>`). Tests in `tests/{checkout,process,sweep}.rs` share `tests/common/mod.rs` (the source repository, the data folder, the pair folder made by `PairLock::take`, `Pair`, `commit_of`), run real git in temp folders and start the built `agent-echo` where cargo put it, never a file a test just wrote; `prepare` and the agent under an inherited `GIT_DIR` run in a child process (`yamt_conflict_repo::run_ignored_in_child`). Depends on `yamt-gitio`, `yamt-pipe` and `yamt-range` only among yamt crates; never tauri, never serde_json (arch-check).
